Reason:
After inet_csk_reqsk_queue_add() adds the child socket to the target listener's accept queue, no sk_data_ready() callback is invoked on nsk. This leaves poll()/epoll_wait() waiters and blocking accept() callers on the target listener unaware of the new connection, causing them to sleep indefinitely.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
