    __NET_INC_STATS(sock_net(nsk),
                    LINUX_MIB_TCPMIGRATEREQSUCCESS);
    reqsk_migrate_reset(req);
    READ_ONCE(nsk->sk_data_ready)(nsk);
} else {
    __NET_INC_STATS(sock_net(nsk),
                    LINUX_MIB_TCPMIGRATEREQFAILURE);
    reqsk_migrate_reset(nreq);
    __reqsk_free(nreq);
}
rcu_read_unlock();
Reason:
Calling READ_ONCE(nsk->sk_data_ready)(nsk) after the successful migration wakes up any waiters on the target listener (poll/epoll/blocking accept). The surrounding rcu_read_lock()/unlock() ensures that nsk remains valid during the dereferences, because the ref held by reuseport_migrate_sock() is transferred to nreq->rsk_listener and the listener uses SOCK_RCU_FREE. This protection is also needed for the sock_net(nsk) access in the statistics counter.

